WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.910
As you might have noticed, the Marvel Cinematic
Universe is big and getting bigger these days.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.930
However, the sheer level of talent that's
involved in bringing all those superheroes

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.480
and villains on screens both big and small
is even bigger.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.770
The list of Academy Award winners who have
either appeared in a MCU movie or that are

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:23.180
set to do so in the near future is currently
comprised of no less than 26 actors, according

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:24.369
to IGN.

00:00:24.369 --> 00:00:28.689
That number should give you a rough idea about
the overall caliber of talent behind the many

00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:31.100
Marvel characters to grace the silver screen.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.800
Of course, there are still plenty of great
actors who haven't joined the MCU in any capacity

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.140
yet, and fans are often speculating about
the next big-name addition to the sprawling

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.430
mega-franchise.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:45.950
He might not have an Oscar to his name yet,
but Keanu Reeves is one of the biggest names

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.489
who tend to come up in such conversations.

00:00:48.489 --> 00:00:52.829
He's easily one of the biggest action movie
actors who has yet to attach their names to

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:57.239
a Marvel Studios project, which seems all
the more glaring when you remember that his

00:00:57.239 --> 00:01:01.789
two most famous roles — Neo in "The Matrix"
movies and the titular character of the "John

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:04.649
Wick" franchise — are essentially superheroes
themselves.

00:01:04.649 --> 00:01:08.560
"He was the one you sent to kill the f---ing
Boogeyman."

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:13.429
Reeves and the MCU seem like a perfect fit,
but is there any chance for this match made

00:01:13.429 --> 00:01:15.909
in tentpole movie heaven to ever happen?

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:20.500
Now, the actor has finally weighed in on whether
he'd ever join the Marvel Cinematic universe

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.850
in a video interview with Esquire.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.020
While fielding questions about roles from
throughout his career, Reeves had a surprisingly

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:31.561
straightforward answer in response to Esquire
asking him outright whether or not a Marvel

00:01:31.561 --> 00:01:33.850
film role might be in his future.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:38.319
First of all, Reeves noted that the word "universe"
is starting to fail to adequately account

00:01:38.319 --> 00:01:40.529
for the true scope of the MCU, saying,

00:01:40.529 --> 00:01:42.420
"Isn't it bigger than a universe?

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.420
It's almost like a Multiverse.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.009
It's a Marvel-verse."

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:49.299
However, he ultimately didn't dodge the question
about becoming a part of that world himself,

00:01:49.299 --> 00:01:50.299
saying,

00:01:50.299 --> 00:01:51.479
"It would be an honor."

00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:56.169
He then spoke to the quality of talent involved
behind the scenes of many of Marvel's flagship

00:01:56.169 --> 00:01:57.169
projects, saying,

00:01:57.169 --> 00:02:00.969
"There's some really amazing directors and
visionaries, and they're doing something that

00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:02.889
no one's really ever done.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:06.529
It's special in that sense, in terms of the
scale, the ambition, the production.

00:02:06.529 --> 00:02:08.509
So it would be cool to be a part of that."

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:13.059
All in all, it appears that Reeves is, at
the very least, not yet a part of an MCU project

00:02:13.059 --> 00:02:17.069
— or if he is, he's clearly not at liberty
to share the news with the public yet.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:21.269
Nevertheless, he appears to be about as open
as an actor could be to the prospect of joining

00:02:21.269 --> 00:02:26.829
Marvel's multibillion dollar franchise, meaning
that his eventual MCU debut remains a distinct,

00:02:26.829 --> 00:02:28.219
enticing possibility.

00:02:28.219 --> 00:02:33.810
"People keep asking me if I'm back, and I
haven't really had an answer.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:37.579
But now, yeah, I'm thinking I'm back."

00:02:37.579 --> 00:02:42.290
It's fascinating that Keanu Reeves actually
addressed the MCU rumors, and doubly so because

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:43.670
he didn't shoot them down.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:48.049
After all, speculation of his involvement
in some upcoming MCU project has been running

00:02:48.049 --> 00:02:49.819
rampant for years now.

00:02:49.819 --> 00:02:53.200
Take the rumor that made the rounds in March
2020, for example.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.329
It suggested that Reeves might become the
MCU incarnation of Ghost Rider.

00:02:57.329 --> 00:03:01.690
The skull-faced, flaming motorcycle rider
might be an interesting choice, seeing as

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:05.870
a version of the character has already made
an appearance in the MCU-adjacent "Agents

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:10.620
of SHIELD," portrayed by Gabriel Luna — though
Reeves would probably portray the Johnny Blaze

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.519
version of the character, which was memorably
played by Nicolas Cage in the decidedly non-MCU

00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:21.349
2007 movie "Ghost Rider," and its buckwild
sequel, "Ghost Rider: Spirit of Vengeance."

00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:26.060
A recent Looper poll, meanwhile, determined
that fans want Reeves to portray the superhuman

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.500
Adam Warlock.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:31.730
That role, of course, ultimately went to "Midsommar"
star Will Poulter, but there's plenty of reason

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:35.709
to assume that the rumor mill will keep turning
for quite a while.

